{{!--
  Eiserne Zeit — the back of every card type.

  Deliberately the same nesting as front.hbs:

      .card-root > .ez-head > .ez-band > .card-title
                 > .card-content-container > .card-body-scalable > .ez-logo-band
                 > .ez-foot > .ez-torn + .ez-foot-label
                 > .ez-side-ref

  so that ONE rule in game-system.css serves the logo on both faces — there
  is no second logo path for the back. If you find yourself writing one, the
  two templates have drifted apart.

  The file still cannot be the front character for character: it renders when
  the card does NOT overflow, and would then print the title and the card
  text a second time. Its body therefore carries only the logo — the only
  coloured element of the whole system. When the card overflows, the engine
  replaces this face with a copy of the front (`back-then-cards`), and the
  logo stands there as the body's last block instead. Whenever this file IS
  rendered it is the last face, so the logo needs no condition here.

  The head band runs at half height on the back, as on every face after the
  first: the title is a reminder there, not an announcement.
--}}
<div class="card-root card-back eiserne-zeit {{card-type}}-card">

  <div class="ez-head">
    <div class="ez-band">
      <div class="card-title"><span class="text-scalable">{{slot "head-title" plain=true}}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ez-torn ez-torn-backhead"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card-content-container">
    <div class="card-body-scalable">
      <div class="ez-logo-band">
        <img class="ez-logo" src="{{asset "assets/eiserne-zeit-logo.png"}}" alt="" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ez-foot">
    <div class="ez-torn ez-torn-foot"></div>
    <div class="ez-foot-label"><span class="text-scalable">{{slot "foot-label" plain=true fallback=(t "back-label")}}</span></div>
  </div>

  {{#if (slot "side-reference")}}
  <div class="ez-side-ref">{{slot "side-reference" markdown=false}}</div>
  {{/if}}

</div>
